$\lim _{x \rightarrow 1} \frac{F(x)-F(1)}{x-1}$
We know, $\lim _{x \rightarrow a} \frac{F(n)-F(a)}{x-a}=F^{\prime}(a)\begin{aligned}
& \therefore F^{\prime}(x)=\frac{d}{d x}\left(\sqrt{9-x^2}\right) \\
& =\frac{1(0-2 x)}{2 \sqrt{9-x^2}}=\frac{-x}{\sqrt{9-x^2}} \\
& F^{\prime}(1)=\frac{-1}{\sqrt{9-1}}=\frac{-1}{\sqrt{8}}=\frac{-1}{2 \sqrt{2}}
\end{aligned}$
